      "seed": 2136783974,
      "version": 731,
      "versionNonce": 268402682,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793652736419,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Generating E-Tags - some approaches\n    - SQL Server - `rowversion` \n        - update vendors set .... where id = request.id, and rowversion=etag\n        - if you get a 0 rows affected, it didn't match, etc.\n\n\n- POST if a 201 should have an e-tag\n    - return the e-tag for the entity you are returning (body)\n- GET by ID should have an e-tag\n    - return an e-tag\n\n- Conditional Get Requests\n    - this is up to you. for most API interactions, the cost is the round trip,\n       so don't do this unless the response is complicated to return\n- Conditional Mutations\n    - I do this ALL the time (PUT, DELETE) - \n    - \"Only do this to this resource if I'm working from the latest copy\"\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Generating E-Tags - some approaches\n    - SQL Server - `rowversion` \n        - update vendors set .... where id = request.id, and rowversion=etag\n        - if you get a 0 rows affected, it didn't match, etc.\n\n\n- POST if a 201 should have an e-tag\n    - return the e-tag for the entity you are returning (body)\n- GET by ID should have an e-tag\n    - return an e-tag\n\n- Conditional Get Requests\n    - this is up to you. for most API interactions, the cost is the round trip,\n       so don't do this unless the response is complicated to return\n- Conditional Mutations\n    - I do this ALL the time (PUT, DELETE) - \n    - \"Only do this to this resource if I'm working from the latest copy\"\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
